 "reconciliation": "ALL EIGHTEEN columns this leaf carries a figure for close exactly, residual zero on every one: eight free-white male, seven free-white female, two free coloured, and the two columns whose footing is blank against a stray mark in the body. The footings on this leaf are crisp where printed 212's are faint, and they are what fixes the enumerator's numeral alphabet for BOTH sheets: f_10_15 closes at 3 against a bold curl over an open bowl, m_u5 at 4 against two parallel diagonals, f_u5 at 6 against an elongated slanted loop. Those three forms are then what the ambiguous cells of both leaves are read against. THE FREE COLOURED BLOCK IS NOT EMPTY: the footing row carries two figures, a 1 in females under 10 and a 1 in females 10 under 24, and both written marks stand on line 2 - a household of six free white persons with two free coloured females in it.",
